__pycache__
*.pyc
.venv
client_data/
logs/
.git
*.env
!*.env.example
.claude/
# Both images copy named files only, so the working tree does not reach /app
# through their COPY lines; this list still bounds the BUILD CONTEXT (and any
# directory a COPY names, e.g. static/). Git-ignoring a file keeps it out of
# the REPOSITORY, which is not the same thing as keeping it out of the build.
# Anything describing the product's own security posture belongs here.
docs/security/
# Note on the pattern below: Docker's `*` does not cross `/`, so this excludes
# a TOP-LEVEL document only. A document inside a directory is covered by that
# directory's own entry (the line above), not by this one. Read it as a floor,
# not as a guarantee that no document anywhere can ship.
*.docx
# Editor and tool state. Neither is needed at run time and both are whatever
# the last person to open the repository happened to have.
.pytest_cache/
.vscode/
